<title>UK: Southern electric cuts prices by average 7..</title>
<headline>Southern electric cuts prices by average 7..</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Electric plc said on Tuesday it was cutting electricity prices by an average of 7.2 percent for all its 2.6 million customers from April 1.  </p>
<p>The company said it was the fifth straight year it had cut prices and followed a price cut of four percent in July.</p>
<p>It said its prices are now some 26 percent lower than they were in 1991 after taking inflation into account.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
